I have a script that first uses commands from the OpenStreetMap package to create maps of location data, then the ctmm package to calculate home range sizes. The ctmm package interferes with OpenStreetMap, so I have to load ctmm after I run the OpenStreetMap code. The issue is that R keeps automatically loading ctmm as soon as I open the program. Once ctmm has automatically loaded, I can't successfully run my script without uninstalling ctmm so it won't automatically load again, and then close out of R before restarting it. Simply offloading the ctmm package won't work for some reason, I have to uninstall it every time it's automatically loaded. As per an online forum, I tried going to tools>global options>restore .RData into workspace at startup and unchecking this option, though the ctmm package continues to automatically load every time. Does anyone have any suggestions for how to prevent the ctmm package from automatically loading every time I open R? Thanks!

